WEBVTT

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.100
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.070
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.840
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.540
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.410
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.610
You just barely escaped with your life

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.940
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:43.210
We're thirsty

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.140
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.350
Extremities and infinity

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.480
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.710
Together, they form a fantasy

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.380
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.580
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.410
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:52.640
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.640
<i>Wink</i>

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.710
Wink

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.530
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.660
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.960
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.570
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.770
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:15.470
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:15.710
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:22.780
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:22.980
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:27.250
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:27.450
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:31.720
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.790
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:36.090
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:36.230
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:44.520
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:45.070
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:47.040
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.240
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.040
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.210
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.710
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.980
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.340
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.650
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:04.880
<i>Shell of Illusion</i>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.500
Pops!

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.300
Above you!

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.440
What? Whoa, whoa!

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.500
Mr. Kurokawa!

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.050
A jumper?

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.580
Splash... Hey...

00:02:33.580 --> 00:02:36.850
That was close. He was about to
take me with him.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.760
Him...

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.160
Again!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.260
Miss Mikura!

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:48.500
Look after Asami for me!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.400
Say what? Hey!

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.490
Mikura?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:55.390
Sorry! Get out of the way!

00:02:58.870 --> 00:02:59.810
Hey!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.680
Why are you targeting Pops?

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.590
Tell me why!

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.380
I'll shoot.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.640
What?

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.730
Where are you?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.640
I'm going to take Asami home.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.480
Pops is there, right? I'll be right back.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.840
Hey, Mikura, what's going...

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:49.620
Gasp, gasp, wheeze, wheeze, what am I?
A pregnant woman?

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.630
I narrowly escaped him taking me
with him on his suicide.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:56.430
This might have been a little too shocking
for Asami. Poor thing.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.230
You'll catch a cold if you don't dry off, Foxy.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.370
Yeah, I'm heading straight to the shower.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:10.600
There's no way she could have been shocked
by something like that, could she?

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.540
Mikura isn't like that.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.000
Well, I'm just glad it looks like she's doing fine.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.700
What?

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.800
Here.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:45.450
<i>Play</i>

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:40.610
I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.050
I thought you might be worried about me,
so I sent this video.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.010
Anyway, talk to you later.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.210
By the way, I've been thinking
about this for a while.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.790
Isn't Asami in love with you?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:56.760
What?! You're kidding me!

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:00.100
The expression on your face tells me
you're not altogether against that idea.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:03.090
Look here, she's in elementary school!

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.170
That was close!

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.330
Yeesh...

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.670
Phantom?

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:23.810
"I'm going to commission an execution
from the Phantom. Be cursed, and die."

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.150
What's this Phantom, anyway?

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.920
A killer.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.550
Of the five people who received that e-mail,
four have already been killed.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:37.400
Oh, my, from an important person
in a high-tech company

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.470
to the chairman of
a telecommunications company...

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:41.970
That's quite a collection of members.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.710
The only one remaining is our old boss.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.470
The killer's so skilled, no one's seen his face.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:52.050
As an exception, the chairman's girlfriend
was with him when he was killed,

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:54.540
but she hung herself from the shock.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.720
Excuse me, I'll ask, just in case.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.210
You're not asking us to play bodyguard
to your boss now, are you?

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:05.120
What the hell kind of business
do you think we're in?

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.260
Well, you certainly aren't short
on security guards.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.000
So?

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:20.610
You're in the business of dangerous
activities, aren't you?

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.200
Well, yes.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.150
Then get killed in place of our boss.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.310
Say what?

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:30.680
Get killed?

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:36.150
That's right.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:39.830
Phantom, is it?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:41.300
You know about him?

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.670
Well, I can't exactly put my finger on it,
but it sounds familiar.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.000
So, this killer known as Phantom,

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.630
how does he make his move?

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.880
It's simple and clear.
Ready for the explanation?

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:58.050
Kill by stabbing the target in the back,
or firing a gun at close range.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.050
Bypassing impregnable security,
and at close range...

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.950
He's extremely confident.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.550
No matter where you're hiding, he sneaks in.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.990
In addition, he doesn't leave any
traces of sneaking in.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:13.520
Phantom... Calling him a ghost
isn't just for appearance's sake.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.400
Ate all the noodles, drank all the soup.
Good meal. Anyway.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:22.670
In order to escape from Phantom,

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:26.440
you need to commit suicide
or fall into his hands. That's why...

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:28.710
There's no choice but to get killed.

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:31.810
The boss of that group certainly
seems like he's very afraid.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:36.880
The young boss I met today is in a rage,
saying he'll capture Phantom.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:39.590
So we were commissioned to be a decoy.

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:42.420
Can't they use a dummy android
or something?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.900
Someone already tried that, but the dummy
went untouched. Didn't do any good.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.800
The actual person was simply shot
and there was quite a bit of damage.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.070
Mr. Kurokawa, isn't this one quite dangerous?

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:56.260
At least, that's how I seriously
feel about this one.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:57.670
Hey!

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:58.610
Hey, let go!

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:00.880
What are you saying? If we chicken out now,

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:03.610
our reputation in the business of
dangerous activities is ruined!

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.180
Splendid! Well said, Mikura!

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:06.850
I have to hand it to the battleship-sized
salmon roe sushi!

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:09.250
I am so excited! Bring it on!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.250
Yay!

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.650
Yay!

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:13.480
So who's going to get killed?

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:21.630
Oh, go a little easy. Especially the front,
since I don't have much there.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:24.430
Yes, yes, of course. Are you going somewhere?

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.970
No, I'm going to be hospitalized.

00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:28.140
I want to make a good impression
on the angel dressed in white.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.670
Cucumbers are okay, but eggplants too.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.670
Hospitalized? Is there something wrong?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:35.180
No, it's more like a check-up hospitalization.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:36.880
I'll come visit you.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.080
Oh, no. It's nothing serious,
so you don't have to do that.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.580
Oh, please don't say that.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.580
We're friends, aren't we?

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:56.020
Yuuzoh Higure

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.400
Time to take your temperature.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.100
5, 9, 6, 3, thank you very much.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.550
If you talk, people will see right through you.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:12.410
Oops!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.950
So it's me, after all?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.050
So that boss is constantly hospitalized
due to diabetes and arthritis, right?

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.220
All you have to do is lie down, so it'll be easy.

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:23.930
Easy, you say...

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.790
What happens if I get killed?

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.160
If you say that,

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:30.200
our reputation in the business
of dangerous activities is ruined.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.260
Oh, I just want to cry and blow my nose.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:36.900
Okay! I'll take your temperature,
so please stick your butt out.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.310
My butt?! No way!

00:09:39.310 --> 00:09:42.240
Don't take me seriously. Here.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.110
Could you cut that out?

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.100
In your case, there's no buffer between
being serious and joking around.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.190
The sensors are A-OK.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:58.630
Gotcha. If something happens,
contact me immediately.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.620
Roger.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.670
Hachisu, how's the old man?

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.610
He just went to sleep. I'll send a video.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.380
All right, give my regards to the doctor as well.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:26.480
Yes, Sir.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:27.910
Doctor.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.390
This situation will continue until
things settle down,

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.980
so please bear with us.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:36.460
If he's going to show up, today, with the office
being closed, would be the most likely.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.100
Sir, is it all right to leave this thing
in that group's hands?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:45.710
Dad's so shaken up, he said he'd
retire and live in Tahiti.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:49.870
I won't let him. I'll get that guy instead!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.370
Even if it means, in the worst case scenario,
that those guys get killed in his place.

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:58.050
I see! So that's how it is.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:01.020
If you can use something,
you might as well use it.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:05.650
Anything?

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.820
So far, there's no sign of anyone
having come in.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.230
What is it?

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.740
Well, you wearing that makes you look
like a completely different person.

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:21.640
Does it look good on me?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.070
The hell I would know.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.310
What happened?

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.500
Unregistered? It's not a guard!

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.180
I'll head over to Pops!

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:31.550
Mikura, be careful!

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:34.040
Damn! Hello? Hello!

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.060
It's not a new employee, but an intruder?
It's too soon.

00:12:47.230 --> 00:12:48.160
Already?

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.480
Time for your medical checkup.

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:03.710
Oh, it's you.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:08.920
If you try to surprise me, I can get scary. So?

00:13:08.920 --> 00:13:10.620
We don't know who yet.

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.550
I'm really counting on you.

00:13:11.550 --> 00:13:14.320
If the guy who's supposed to get killed really
does die, it's all meaningless, understand?

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:18.520
Just now...

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.600
The real one got shot.

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:22.760
You're kidding me!

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.530
Lock down the exits! Move in pairs!

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:30.770
Sir!

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:32.170
Son of a bitch!

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:34.930
Son of a bitch!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:37.410
There!

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.080
That's Hachisu's cell phone.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.620
Is he going after the Phantom?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.880
All right, the roof! Head to the roof!

00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:47.560
The roof?

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:52.050
Then who the hell is the guy that's
hanging around down here?

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.330
Mikura, come back.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:02.400
Cleaning things up isn't our job.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:04.700
What? But...

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:13.080
What's the matter, Pops? Hey, Pops!

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:17.310
Mr. Kurokawa!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.620
Mr. Kurokawa! Mr. Kurokawa!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.800
That was close.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.630
What the hell's the meaning of this, anyway?

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.630
If you move, you won't live
long enough to eat dinner.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.100
You!

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.370
Hey, wait...

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:32.230
He's Phantom?

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:34.960
Seems like it. Where's Mikura?

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:40.630
Run!

00:15:42.440 --> 00:15:43.400
Not good!

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:53.650
He was cornered, so he blew himself up?

00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:55.810
Sure didn't put up much of a fight.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.840
So what was the deal with the guy
who attacked you?

00:15:59.250 --> 00:16:00.150
Mikura!

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:01.120
Damn!

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:03.510
Mikura!

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.250
Mikura...

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:18.010
Everything's all right over here. How's Dad?

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.540
Oh, he's resting quietly.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.240
You sure are a tricky bastard.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.780
The one at the hospital was
a body double and all.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:27.450
Considering who we were dealing with, yeah.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:29.540
The only ones who knew were me and Dad.

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.750
However, now that we know Phantom
isn't just one person,

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:35.460
just in case, we'll have a funeral,

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:37.390
but don't let your guard down either.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.990
I understand. Anyway, talk to you later.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.630
What's that?

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.670
Damn, we were a decoy for a decoy.
They sure made a mockery of us.

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:49.440
Well, we were given our pay
on top of Mikura's compensation,

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.200
so we got quite a bit from this job.
Isn't this great? After us, the deluge.

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:56.780
But those four guys and the big boss,
who all received that e-mail...

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:59.010
What did they do to get that kind
of grudge against them?

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.570
Do you know what a liquid crystal
communication system is?

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:09.090
To put it simply, it's a system
where the liquid crystal itself

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.260
becomes a camera and a microphone, right?

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.330
Thanks to this system, we can
see each other while talking.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.330
It's a world-class invention.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:19.530
Apparently, it was developed
by a private individual

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.900
and then stolen from him.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:22.960
Stolen?

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:27.240
Those four were involved in that
and made quite a bit.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.940
The person who this was stolen from...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:33.550
His name seems to be Ozuma,
but his whereabouts are unknown.

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:34.850
Ozuma?!

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:39.810
Something Ozuma. His first name
was Yuuichiro, I think.

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:44.730
<i>Search
